Famotidine oral suspension is a medicament put up in measured doses or in forms for retail sale, so it falls in heading 3004. Famotidine is a thiazole-ring compound, so it would not fall under the subheadings for antibiotics, hormones, or alkaloids. It therefore goes in the "Other" subheading 3004.90.

Within 3004.90, HTS 3004.90.92 is the "Other" statistical grouping. The common 10-digit codes are 3004.90.9290 for other medicaments and 3004.90.9250 for those for... I'm not certain of the exact statistical suffix. Many famotidine imports are entered under 3004.90.9290, so I'll use that.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9290", "reason": "Famotidine oral suspension is a retail-packaged, dosed medicament of heading 3004 that does not fit any specific subheading (not an antibiotic, hormone, or alkaloid), so it falls under the residual 'other' medicaments provision."}
